WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }
::cue(c.credits) { color: #a8c7fa; font-size: 78%; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:04.780
Fight, crash through, and face the challenge!

3
00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:08.000
These are our hard knock days.

4
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.830
Can't quench our thirst with a peaceful, everyday life.

5
00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:15.340
Here we go - don't ever run away!

6
00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:19.380
Let's go on living as the mighty winds take us!

7
00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:21.870
We've still got so far to go.

8
00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:26.390
Gotta keep going through the hard knock days.

9
00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:31.610
Let's do it again, yes, baby. How many times

10
00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:34.110
do I have to stand back up to make my dream come true?

11
00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:36.730
Feels like the strength of my resolve

12
00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:39.200
is put to the test everyday.

13
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:40.700
Hey, let's go!

14
00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:44.450
I don't want to make excuses and settle for being mediocre.

15
00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:45.960
Hey, let's go!

16
00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:49.670
We leapt into a crazy, lawless world.

17
00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:54.170
As I struggled for a foothold, reality caught me off guard.

18
00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:59.470
Even if it beats me, hits me, knocks me down again,

19
00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:00.220
Oh!

20
00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:04.560
Only when we get back on our feet and look forward,

21
00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:07.450
will we have the last laugh, be the winners!

22
00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:10.120
We gotta go down this glory road, till we reach our goal!

23
00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:12.720
Fight, shake it off, act strong!

24
00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:15.720
These are our hard knock days.

25
00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:20.730
There's no such thing as a safe choice.

26
00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:23.060
Here we go - we'll always be the strongest!

27
00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:27.320
Let's keep moving - never mind the consequences.

28
00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:29.900
Let's put our wishes all together,

29
00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:34.910
and keep on going through the hard knock days.

30
00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:45.530
<b>Zoro vs. Pica</b>

31
00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:55.340
<b>Dressrosa















SMILE Factory</b>

32
00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:04.040
Now, you guys!

33
00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:07.080
Are you ready?!

34
00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:09.680
Yeah!

35
00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:16.400
Take this despicable factory that caused you Tontattans so much pain...

36
00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:19.460
and tear it down!

37
00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:24.060
Let's go!

38
00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:27.020
Thank you, Fraland!

39
00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:31.740
Tontattans, good luck...

40
00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:40.140
You handle the mess up there...

41
00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:41.880
Luffy.

42
00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:00.480
Help the injured first! Call the rescue team!

43
00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:01.160
Aye!

44
00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:04.010
<b>Royal Palace Grounds</b>

45
00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:10.470
Showtime!

46
00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:18.250
Half Moon...

47
00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:19.710
Glaive!

48
00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:24.000
<b>Fourth Step















Sunflower Field</b>

49
00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.170
<b>Kyros 
vs.
Diamante</b>

50
00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:25.730
Kyros!

51
00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:29.770
Just now, you were lashing out at me in rage.

52
00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:32.870
Have you forgotten your place?

53
00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:40.770
Did you think that I'm merely a talented matador who can make things ripple?!

54
00:03:41.350 --> 00:03:46.590
You couldn't remain the Colosseum's strongest warrior forever, you know!

55
00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:49.930
My skill is indisputable.

56
00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:56.970
The current hero of the Colosseum is me, Diamante-sama!

57
00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:01.050
I don't care about that title!

58
00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:04.290
Of course, the rippling does help.

59
00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:15.730
Father!

60
00:04:17.050 --> 00:04:20.310
Nice try! You almost had me!

61
00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:26.970
Well, of course it would come to this.

62
00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:30.250
You've been running around the country all day,

63
00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:35.230
and fighting me on this rippling arena while trying to keep your daughter safe!

64
00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:37.840
And on just one leg, at that!

65
00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:41.070
An ordinary person would have long since stopped moving.

66
00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:45.650
Don't worry about my leg.

67
00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:51.730
If I wanted to use it as an excuse,
I wouldn't have come to this battlefield!

68
00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:57.350
I'm proud of my missing leg!
I gave it up for the man who saved my life!

69
00:04:57.630 --> 00:05:01.470
I see. Then, I'll gladly aim for your weak spot.

70
00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:08.730
It'd be no fun to kill you the old-fashioned way,
now that you're so worn out.

71
00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:12.330
How about a game?!

72
00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:20.370
The last showtime!

73
00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:27.150
Is that...

74
00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:28.750
Confetti?

75
00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:30.070
That's right!

76
00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:35.090
It's something that looks like paper, thanks to my ripple power.

77
00:05:35.970 --> 00:05:39.010
And now, I'll undo my power.

78
00:05:40.030 --> 00:05:41.820
Ripple Release!

79
00:05:44.270 --> 00:05:45.770
Spiked iron balls!

80
00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:51.530
Gaze upon their beauty! They're like stardust!

81
00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:52.970
Robin-san!

82
00:05:53.090 --> 00:05:54.710
Doesn't look like we can avoid it.

83
00:05:54.890 --> 00:05:57.150
Robiland, please protect Rebecca!

84
00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:59.870
Commander-san, you're in danger too!

85
00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:02.190
I'll be fine!

86
00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:06.390
You're panicking, I see. Very perceptive of you.

87
00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:12.150
Yes, this stardust can slaughter entire armies!

88
00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:15.330
It'd take a miracle for you to survive.

89
00:06:15.510 --> 00:06:17.740
Thank goodness we're at the Sunflower Field.

90
00:06:18.030 --> 00:06:19.240
Mil Fleur!
Thousand Flower

91
00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:25.550
I'm sorry I have to pluck such magnificent flowers.

92
00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:31.960
Struggle all you want!

93
00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:34.570
Adios!

94
00:06:34.810 --> 00:06:37.270
Death Enjambre!

95
00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:37.270
Death Swarm

96
00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:45.770
Flower Umbrella!

97
00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:49.220
That was close!

98
00:06:49.670 --> 00:06:52.090
Oh? Quite impressive.

99
00:06:52.210 --> 00:06:53.230
Pay attention!

100
00:06:56.590 --> 00:06:58.930
Kyros!

101
00:06:59.050 --> 00:07:03.770
If an army were to fall to this kind of attack,
they'd be truly pathetic!

102
00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:05.990
That's so crazy!

103
00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:09.330
He's swatting away every single spiked iron ball!

104
00:07:10.870 --> 00:07:14.430
Can he make it through a rain shower without even getting wet?!

105
00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:15.330
Dammit!

106
00:07:26.890 --> 00:07:29.090
Father!

107
00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:33.930
Look out above, Kyros!

108
00:07:34.190 --> 00:07:38.650
You klutz! How could you trip now?

109
00:07:38.790 --> 00:07:41.740
Damn you, Diamante! I'll get you!

110
00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:43.840
No, Rebecca! They're still falling!

111
00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:47.570
Father!

112
00:07:47.670 --> 00:07:48.670
You'll pay for this!

113
00:07:49.270 --> 00:07:52.010
You'll pay for everything, Diamante!

114
00:07:53.590 --> 00:07:57.350
Well said, Rebecca! Go ahead, make me pay!

115
00:07:57.490 --> 00:08:00.670
Fight me! I'll kill you with my own two hands!

116
00:08:00.890 --> 00:08:02.850
Just like I did your mother!

117
00:08:02.970 --> 00:08:06.810
Let go of me, Robin-san! I'll kill him!

118
00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:16.150
How long will this last?! The Flower Umbrella can't take any more!

119
00:08:19.670 --> 00:08:22.770
Diamante!

120
00:08:36.270 --> 00:08:39.430
This is my fight, Rebecca!

121
00:08:39.630 --> 00:08:40.810
Drop...

122
00:08:41.810 --> 00:08:43.290
your sword!

123
00:08:45.770 --> 00:08:49.850
For an entire decade...

124
00:08:49.950 --> 00:08:53.350
Father! Get under the umbrella! You'll die!

125
00:08:53.530 --> 00:08:57.490
...you have followed your mother's wish!

126
00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:02.130
Mother said that it's bad to hurt people.

127
00:09:02.290 --> 00:09:04.950
I'm teaching you this so that you don't get hurt.

128
00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:08.950
She's never hurt anyone,

129
00:09:09.070 --> 00:09:11.790
and she's won all her battles by ring out!

130
00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:13.710
She's the undefeated woman!

131
00:09:15.350 --> 00:09:18.410
You can't even cut your enemy and you call yourself a winner?!

132
00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:20.010
Shed some blood, Rebecca!

133
00:09:20.150 --> 00:09:22.130
You coward!

134
00:09:22.770 --> 00:09:25.030
That match was a complete disgrace!

135
00:09:25.510 --> 00:09:27.900
You're the shame of all gladiators!

136
00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:30.980
Drop dead, Rebecca!

137
00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:33.030
Your family's a bunch of monsters!

138
00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:35.290
You foul-blooded wench!

139
00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:43.820
You've been fighting in the Colosseum, but you still haven't hurt anybody!

140
00:09:46.170 --> 00:09:49.440
Your hands are still beautiful!

141
00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:51.510
Those are the hands...

142
00:09:53.850 --> 00:09:56.630
in which your mother Scarlett's spirit lives!

143
00:10:02.670 --> 00:10:03.990
Mother...

144
00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:11.390
After all your efforts, there's no need to bathe them in the blood of a devil like him.

145
00:10:18.450 --> 00:10:19.510
Rebecca!

146
00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:23.490
I'll make sure you never have to swing your sword again!

147
00:10:41.230 --> 00:10:42.990
Kyros!

148
00:10:43.430 --> 00:10:47.190
Are you made of iron?!

149
00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:56.540
No, this guy is beyond insane...

150
00:11:03.650 --> 00:11:04.790
The pain...

151
00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:09.480
The pain is proof that I am human!

152
00:11:09.900 --> 00:11:12.700
You people would never understand...

153
00:11:15.560 --> 00:11:20.000
The despair of being forgotten by the ones you love!

154
00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:23.000
Scarlett!

155
00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:28.900
Why? Why didn't you wait for me?!

156
00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:33.100
Of course.

157
00:11:33.820 --> 00:11:36.400
I must have disappeared from your mind, too.

158
00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:40.940
Both our promise... and our time together...

159
00:11:44.340 --> 00:11:46.700
I don't know who you are...

160
00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:49.000
It's me! It's Kyros!

161
00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:51.170
Please...

162
00:11:55.600 --> 00:12:01.720
With these tin arms,
I can't even feel your fading warmth!

163
00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:15.600
You people don't understand...

164
00:12:16.030 --> 00:12:20.260
The agony of being unable to feel anything you touch!

165
00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:25.160
Or the tragedies that have befallen Dressrosa...
Compared to them,

166
00:12:26.020 --> 00:12:28.840
this is not even pain!

167
00:12:32.700 --> 00:12:34.540
If you want to say I'm made of something,

168
00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:41.120
then I'll become this country's fury incarnate...

169
00:12:43.970 --> 00:12:45.700
and bring you down!

170
00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:52.420
How is he this strong?!

171
00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:59.360
Your glory days were twenty years ago!

172
00:13:02.120 --> 00:13:06.020
Don't underestimate my true skill with the sword!

173
00:13:09.780 --> 00:13:13.400
You're still not dead?! You damn monster!

174
00:13:24.760 --> 00:13:27.600
Just as the iron rain lifted, too.

175
00:13:29.820 --> 00:13:34.540
I'll end this by killing you myself.

176
00:13:34.680 --> 00:13:39.840
Just like Scarlett, who you two loved so much!

177
00:13:50.700 --> 00:13:53.170
Diamante, you fiend!

178
00:13:53.740 --> 00:13:55.600
How dare you bring up my sister again!

179
00:13:57.060 --> 00:13:59.200
Damn you, Diamante!

180
00:14:01.540 --> 00:14:04.080
I'm sorry, King Riku!

181
00:14:04.620 --> 00:14:09.560
We searched as hard as we could, but all for naught! A man named Diamante got there before us,

182
00:14:10.010 --> 00:14:13.400
and we found Scarlett-sama lying in the streets,

183
00:14:13.940 --> 00:14:15.260
shot to death!

184
00:14:19.520 --> 00:14:20.900
You killed my sister?!

185
00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:24.360
Oh yeah, she was your older sister!

186
00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:28.300
She was buying food at a market in the town.

187
00:14:28.540 --> 00:14:33.830
If the fool could've controlled her hunger,
she wouldn't have had to die!

188
00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:37.020
Let go of me, Tank!

189
00:14:37.260 --> 00:14:40.590
Please stop! Don't do anything rash!

190
00:14:40.680 --> 00:14:42.720
I can't take it anymore!

191
00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:45.560
We'll stay in the palace, too.

192
00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:48.360
To protect you!

193
00:15:04.820 --> 00:15:06.740
Diamante!

194
00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:10.840
My strikes rend the earth itself!

195
00:15:14.540 --> 00:15:16.520
Take this, and that!

196
00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:18.140
There!

197
00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:22.080
Let's hope you can dodge my attacks...

198
00:15:22.180 --> 00:15:24.520
With your single, shot-up leg!

199
00:15:26.260 --> 00:15:28.440
I have no intention of dodging!

200
00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:33.220
If you won't dodge, you're just an idiot!

201
00:15:33.380 --> 00:15:35.300
I will return peace!

202
00:15:35.400 --> 00:15:39.580
Half Moon Glaive!

203
00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:43.760
Trueno...
Thunder

204
00:15:46.240 --> 00:15:48.280
Bastardo!
Bastard

205
00:16:38.630 --> 00:16:41.760
I owe you one, Robiland.

206
00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:10.600
Father!

207
00:17:14.120 --> 00:17:16.480
Father, we must tend to your wounds!

208
00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:29.480
I couldn't protect your mother, but I'll protect you with my life.

209
00:17:30.440 --> 00:17:36.660
Until the day you can find true happiness, I'll always be by your side.

210
00:17:57.850 --> 00:18:00.220
He took down Diamante!

211
00:18:05.370 --> 00:18:08.300
He took down the Diamante?

212
00:18:18.440 --> 00:18:20.980
Is it true, Viola-sama?!

213
00:18:21.180 --> 00:18:24.560
That's right! Kyros won!

214
00:18:24.900 --> 00:18:26.340
Rebecca is okay, too.

215
00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:29.660
Nico Robin protected her.

216
00:18:32.020 --> 00:18:35.620
I can't believe he took down one of the Donquixote Family's top commanders!

217
00:18:36.170 --> 00:18:38.920
He took down the hero of the Colosseum...

218
00:18:39.080 --> 00:18:40.260
That's absurd!

219
00:18:40.700 --> 00:18:44.960
Kyros was the original undefeated hero of the Colosseum!

220
00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:50.600
We thought no one could beat the Donquixote Family...

221
00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:52.880
but they're falling, one by one!

222
00:18:59.620 --> 00:19:00.730
Kyros.

223
00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:04.820
Army Commander Kyros!

224
00:19:13.540 --> 00:19:16.310
Senor Pink lost the battle at the factory...

225
00:19:17.190 --> 00:19:23.200
and many others of the Donquixote Family have been defeated by the warriors siding with Straw Hat Luffy.

226
00:19:25.240 --> 00:19:29.030
There are four major opponents of the Donquixote Family left!

227
00:19:29.970 --> 00:19:31.880
Bellamy the Hyena...

228
00:19:32.300 --> 00:19:36.100
And the two top commanders, Pica and Trebol!

229
00:19:36.180 --> 00:19:37.100
And...

230
00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:42.580
the current king, one of the Seven Warlords of the Sea, Doflamingo!

231
00:19:43.760 --> 00:19:46.800
The Final Four!

232
00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:52.940
Never expected them to make it that far!

233
00:19:53.220 --> 00:19:55.380
The Straw Hat Pirates are incredible!

234
00:19:55.540 --> 00:19:59.950
I can't believe we were trying to save ourselves by killing them!

235
00:20:00.060 --> 00:20:04.060
Well, like they say, we all make mistakes!

236
00:20:04.200 --> 00:20:07.640
As long as you see the error of your ways, I'll forgive you!

237
00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:13.600
Old King Riku, where are you going?

238
00:20:14.300 --> 00:20:16.980
I don't think anyone will try to kill me now.

239
00:20:17.660 --> 00:20:18.810
I'll go down to the town.

240
00:20:19.610 --> 00:20:21.690
Surely there's still something I can do.

241
00:20:22.960 --> 00:20:24.760
I shall accompany you!

242
00:20:25.130 --> 00:20:28.090
I refuse to depend on the Government or the Navy!

243
00:20:29.460 --> 00:20:31.000
Everybody's lost hope.

244
00:20:31.440 --> 00:20:35.560
They think there's no escape from this bird cage, this deadly game!

245
00:20:36.300 --> 00:20:37.740
We should all go too!

246
00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:43.020
Let's tell everybody in the town there's still hope!

247
00:20:47.940 --> 00:20:51.360
It would seem the tides have begun to turn.

248
00:20:55.060 --> 00:20:58.400
Where did the Navy Admiral go?

249
00:20:58.660 --> 00:21:00.720
Did you not notice?

250
00:21:01.020 --> 00:21:03.740
He descended to the ground quite some time ago.

251
00:21:04.300 --> 00:21:08.700
Gather all the citizens in one place.

252
00:21:09.260 --> 00:21:13.860
Somewhere we'll be able to defend them.

253
00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:14.760
Yes, sir!

254
00:21:19.150 --> 00:21:20.300
Is he...

255
00:21:19.650 --> 00:21:22.200
<b>Royal Plateau</b>

256
00:21:23.250 --> 00:21:24.690
That bastard...

257
00:21:27.220 --> 00:21:30.850
<b>Fourth Step















Sunflower Field</b>

258
00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:31.030
Father, what are these tremors?

259
00:21:36.810 --> 00:21:37.810
Rebecca!

260
00:21:39.570 --> 00:21:40.590
That's...

261
00:21:40.990 --> 00:21:44.030
But I thought Zoro was keeping him in check? Pica!

262
00:21:54.070 --> 00:21:55.770
Diamante...

263
00:21:56.250 --> 00:22:00.570
What a sorry state for a Family top commander.

264
00:22:11.910 --> 00:22:12.830
Father!

265
00:22:14.890 --> 00:22:16.160
I should have guessed.

266
00:22:16.890 --> 00:22:20.590
We're not here to fight one-on-one!

267
00:22:21.340 --> 00:22:24.130
As long as the enemy still stands,
the fight won't end!

268
00:22:26.470 --> 00:22:28.940
Don't push yourself, Father!
You can't even move.

269
00:22:29.030 --> 00:22:30.490
Stand down, Rebecca!

270
00:22:31.470 --> 00:22:32.590
I have to ask.

271
00:22:33.410 --> 00:22:36.750
What is King Riku to you people?

272
00:22:37.070 --> 00:22:42.390
Rebecca, you had to endure unending jeers because of him.

273
00:22:44.030 --> 00:22:45.930
If it weren't for him...

274
00:22:46.050 --> 00:22:49.130
What nonsense! You people framed him!

275
00:22:49.720 --> 00:22:53.230
King Riku is my father-in-law,

276
00:22:53.630 --> 00:22:56.350
who stood by me since my days of thuggery!

277
00:22:57.550 --> 00:23:03.390
The Royal Riku Family is revered worldwide as a family that understands the true meaning of peace!

278
00:23:07.470 --> 00:23:10.800
A clear sky, flowers in full bloom...

279
00:23:10.800 --> 00:23:13.800
A great country filled with gentle hearts!

280
00:23:14.600 --> 00:23:17.000
That's what Dressrosa truly is!

281
00:23:20.130 --> 00:23:26.210
Kicking you beasts out and returning him to the throne once more is our nation's desire this very moment!

282
00:23:27.660 --> 00:23:28.980
I understand.

283
00:23:31.870 --> 00:23:34.000
Huh? He vanished?

284
00:23:35.920 --> 00:23:37.490
Charlestone!

285
00:23:41.300 --> 00:23:44.020
Th-The hell is that?! That scared me!

286
00:23:44.360 --> 00:23:46.140
Now he's on the third level!

287
00:23:46.040 --> 00:23:51.700
<b>Second Step</b>

288
00:23:48.180 --> 00:23:51.900
That damn bastard!
He's supposed to fight me!

289
00:23:52.020 --> 00:23:53.360
Does he even want to fight?!

290
00:24:00.160 --> 00:24:04.700
Either way, I can't reach him
if he's moving around in the plateau.

291
00:24:04.900 --> 00:24:07.640
Prepare to die once you're back in range!

292
00:24:07.880 --> 00:24:09.200
Charlestone!

293
00:24:10.860 --> 00:24:12.940
Pica-sama, please stop!

294
00:24:13.260 --> 00:24:14.080
Pica-sama!

295
00:24:14.180 --> 00:24:15.280
Help!

296
00:24:22.540 --> 00:24:24.720
That bastard! He's attacking the injured!

297
00:24:25.520 --> 00:24:28.000
You betrayed us, Baby 5!

298
00:24:28.140 --> 00:24:29.080
Steel Mill!

299
00:24:29.240 --> 00:24:30.260
Look out!

300
00:24:34.720 --> 00:24:35.460
Sai!

301
00:24:35.580 --> 00:24:37.080
Charlestone!

302
00:24:45.620 --> 00:24:47.480
That asshole!

303
00:24:49.380 --> 00:24:50.820
You stony bastard!

304
00:24:51.000 --> 00:24:54.740
That's enough outta you!
Quit going after the injured!

305
00:24:54.860 --> 00:24:56.030
Roronoa.

306
00:24:56.660 --> 00:24:58.000
Bite Stone!

307
00:24:58.080 --> 00:25:00.500
One-Sword Style... Demon Horse!

308
00:25:01.600 --> 00:25:03.860
Say, Roronoa Zoro...

309
00:25:04.060 --> 00:25:07.880
Do you know who's on the old Royal Grounds?

310
00:25:08.400 --> 00:25:09.860
The king of this country!

311
00:25:10.020 --> 00:25:11.000
The former king!

312
00:25:11.620 --> 00:25:13.400
What are you getting at?!

313
00:25:15.700 --> 00:25:17.910
On the old Royal Grounds,

314
00:25:18.020 --> 00:25:21.210
the former senior officials of this country are there,

315
00:25:21.340 --> 00:25:24.360
as well as those samurai and God Usopp.

316
00:25:24.920 --> 00:25:30.300
I heard the whole nation seeks
King Riku's restoration.

317
00:25:30.500 --> 00:25:31.840
So what?!

318
00:25:32.120 --> 00:25:36.740
That pisses me off! Doffy is the one and only king!

319
00:25:49.200 --> 00:25:50.300
What the...

320
00:26:02.160 --> 00:26:03.460
Bastard!

321
00:26:19.560 --> 00:26:21.700
It started to move again!

322
00:26:21.800 --> 00:26:23.620
Wh-What's he going to do?!

323
00:26:30.920 --> 00:26:34.060
This is Donquixote country!

324
00:26:38.530 --> 00:26:39.780
He's walking!

325
00:26:39.920 --> 00:26:41.600
Run!

326
00:26:42.000 --> 00:26:45.440
The statue's started to move! Run! Run for it!

327
00:26:58.520 --> 00:27:00.020
Whoa, whoa, don't tell me...

328
00:27:04.620 --> 00:27:06.060
That bastard!

329
00:27:06.740 --> 00:27:08.500
So he's planning to take out the king?!

330
00:27:12.860 --> 00:27:14.020
Bastard!

331
00:27:14.480 --> 00:27:17.320
So that's why he drove me out this far!

332
00:27:18.840 --> 00:27:20.360
I can't catch up to him!

333
00:27:24.260 --> 00:27:27.720
I totally got played!
Gotta do something, or else...

334
00:27:29.820 --> 00:27:33.540
It'll take him just one punch
to shatter the Royal Grounds!

335
00:27:34.520 --> 00:27:37.240
Usopp and the king'll be crushed to death!

336
00:27:37.380 --> 00:27:39.080
There any way to stop it?

337
00:27:39.080 --> 00:27:40.500
Pirate Hunter!

338
00:27:40.900 --> 00:27:43.500
We won't let you get in Pica-sama's way!

339
00:27:47.500 --> 00:27:49.000
You're a pest!

340
00:27:51.100 --> 00:27:51.870
Zoro!

341
00:27:52.120 --> 00:27:53.140
Not good!

342
00:27:54.520 --> 00:27:56.220
If we let him go, he'll...

343
00:28:00.960 --> 00:28:02.040
Grandfather!

344
00:28:02.180 --> 00:28:03.120
Usopp!

345
00:28:07.080 --> 00:28:09.120
That bastard!

346
00:28:12.200 --> 00:28:16.640
<b>PLAN 1</b>

347
00:28:13.660 --> 00:28:15.020
Plan 1.

348
00:28:14.890 --> 00:28:18.930
<b>LONG DISTANCE SLASH</b>

349
00:28:16.220 --> 00:28:17.920
Long-distance slash.

350
00:28:16.640 --> 00:28:18.930
<b>PLAN 1</b>

351
00:28:25.760 --> 00:28:28.080
No, at that range, it would be far too weak.

352
00:28:28.160 --> 00:28:29.480
It won't take him down.

353
00:28:30.150 --> 00:28:34.840
<b>JUMP</b>
<b>ON TOP</b>
<b>OF HIM</b>
<b>PLAN 2</b>

354
00:28:31.320 --> 00:28:32.520
Plan 2.

355
00:28:32.880 --> 00:28:34.600
Jump on top of him.

356
00:28:39.420 --> 00:28:40.610
Yeah that won't work.

357
00:28:43.980 --> 00:28:46.700
<b>PLAN 3</b>

358
00:28:44.780 --> 00:28:46.610
<b>SHOUT OUT REAL LOUD</b>

359
00:28:44.780 --> 00:28:46.650
<b>TO WARN USOPP</b>

360
00:28:44.820 --> 00:28:46.700
<b>AND THE</b>
<b>OTHERS</b>

361
00:28:44.820 --> 00:28:45.070
<b>PLAN 3 SHOUT OUT REAL LOUD</b>

362
00:28:44.860 --> 00:28:45.030
<b>TO WARN USOPP SHOUT OUT REAL LOUD</b>

363
00:28:44.900 --> 00:28:46.740
<b>DANGER</b>

364
00:28:44.900 --> 00:28:46.780
<b>OF THE</b>

365
00:28:44.900 --> 00:28:45.110
<b>OTHERS AND THE</b>

366
00:28:44.940 --> 00:28:45.190
<b>DANGER OF THE</b>

367
00:28:46.100 --> 00:28:47.380
Plan 3.

368
00:28:46.610 --> 00:28:52.200
<b>SHOUT OUT REAL LOUD</b>

369
00:28:46.650 --> 00:28:52.200
<b>TO WARN USOPP</b>

370
00:28:46.700 --> 00:28:52.200
<b>AND THE</b>
<b>OTHERS</b>
<b>PLAN 3</b>

371
00:28:46.740 --> 00:28:52.200
<b>DANGER</b>

372
00:28:46.780 --> 00:28:52.200
<b>OF THE</b>

373
00:28:47.760 --> 00:28:51.120
Shout out real loud to warn Usopp and the others of the danger.

374
00:28:53.120 --> 00:28:58.180
Usopp!

375
00:29:03.440 --> 00:29:06.720
He'd never hear me from this distance.

376
00:29:09.930 --> 00:29:11.800
<b>AND TELL HIM</b>

377
00:29:09.970 --> 00:29:11.850
<b>"GET THE HELL</b>
<b>BY SNAIL PHONE</b>

378
00:29:10.010 --> 00:29:10.140
<b>AND TELL HIM BY SNAIL PHONE</b>

379
00:29:10.050 --> 00:29:10.180
<b>"GET THE HELL OUTTA THERE"</b>

380
00:29:10.050 --> 00:29:10.260
<b>CALL HIM PLAN 4</b>

381
00:29:10.050 --> 00:29:13.510
<b>OUTTA THERE"</b>

382
00:29:10.090 --> 00:29:13.510
<b>CALL HIM</b>

383
00:29:10.140 --> 00:29:13.600
<b>PLAN 4</b>

384
00:29:10.780 --> 00:29:12.000
Plan 4.

385
00:29:11.800 --> 00:29:16.830
<b>AND TELL HIM</b>

386
00:29:11.850 --> 00:29:16.830
<b>BY SNAIL PHONE</b>
<b>"GET THE HELL</b>

387
00:29:12.680 --> 00:29:15.920
Call him by Snail Phone and tell him,
"Get the hell outta there."

388
00:29:13.510 --> 00:29:16.830
<b>CALL HIM</b>
<b>OUTTA THERE"</b>

389
00:29:13.600 --> 00:29:16.830
<b>PLAN 4</b>

390
00:29:25.420 --> 00:29:27.060
Oh, I don't have one.

391
00:29:29.900 --> 00:29:32.780
Don't come any closer!

392
00:29:35.440 --> 00:29:39.500
And even if I could tell him,
there's no time for everyone to get away!

393
00:29:49.120 --> 00:29:50.440
Go for it!

394
00:29:50.540 --> 00:29:51.760
Pica-sama!

395
00:29:53.960 --> 00:29:55.580
He's going after King Riku!

396
00:29:57.940 --> 00:30:01.120
It's none of our business,
but I still don't like it!

397
00:30:01.300 --> 00:30:04.600
Stop, you stone monster!

398
00:30:04.760 --> 00:30:08.240
Sogeking-senpai is on that plateau!

399
00:30:08.380 --> 00:30:10.820
Stone! Come back here!

400
00:30:10.940 --> 00:30:13.400
I'll fight you!

401
00:30:17.880 --> 00:30:21.440
No!

402
00:30:29.360 --> 00:30:30.560
I understand now!

403
00:30:30.800 --> 00:30:36.480
The Pirate Hunter was right in
telling me to save my King Punch!

404
00:30:42.380 --> 00:30:44.960
I'll save you, King Riku, my old friend!

405
00:30:45.040 --> 00:30:46.760
Wait a sec, King of wherever!

406
00:30:47.260 --> 00:30:48.520
"Wherever"?!

407
00:30:48.680 --> 00:30:52.780
That's "King Elizabello of Prodence" to you, Pirate Hunter!

408
00:30:53.520 --> 00:30:55.900
I told you, it's no use just destroying him.

409
00:30:56.320 --> 00:30:59.500
He'll keep coming back
unless you beat him in the flesh!

410
00:30:59.800 --> 00:31:01.600
Well, what should we do then?

411
00:31:07.280 --> 00:31:10.240
Help me!

412
00:31:12.380 --> 00:31:14.120
Pirate Hunter!

413
00:31:40.300 --> 00:31:41.080
Hey!

414
00:31:41.620 --> 00:31:42.880
Give me two minutes.

415
00:31:45.640 --> 00:31:47.500
Is King Riku there?

416
00:31:53.080 --> 00:31:54.470
Plan 5!

417
00:31:53.120 --> 00:31:54.470
<b>PLAN 5</b>

418
00:31:54.470 --> 00:31:54.850
<b>FLY</b>

419
00:31:54.520 --> 00:31:57.810
Fly into the sky and dice this punk to bits!

420
00:31:54.850 --> 00:31:55.100
<b>INTO</b>

421
00:31:55.100 --> 00:31:55.350
<b>THE</b>

422
00:31:55.350 --> 00:31:55.720
<b>SKY</b>

423
00:31:55.720 --> 00:31:56.100
<b>AND</b>

424
00:31:56.100 --> 00:31:56.350
<b>DICE</b>

425
00:31:56.350 --> 00:31:56.600
<b>THIS</b>

426
00:31:56.600 --> 00:31:56.850
<b>PUNK</b>

427
00:31:56.850 --> 00:31:57.100
<b>TO</b>

428
00:31:57.100 --> 00:31:57.350
<b>BITS</b>

429
00:31:57.810 --> 00:31:59.690
<b>FLY INTO THE SKY</b>
<b>AND DICE HIM</b>
<b>TO BITS!!!</b>

430
00:31:57.810 --> 00:31:59.560
<b>PLAN 5 5</b>

431
00:31:57.850 --> 00:31:58.020
<b>FLY INTO THE SKY AND DICE HIM</b>
<b>PLAN 555</b>

432
00:31:57.890 --> 00:31:58.100
<b>PLAN 5</b>

433
00:31:59.560 --> 00:32:02.710
<b>PLAN 5 5</b>

434
00:31:59.690 --> 00:32:02.710
<b>FLY INTO THE SKY</b>
<b>AND DICE HIM</b>
<b>TO BITS!!!</b>

435
00:32:03.620 --> 00:32:05.320
That'll work!

436
00:32:20.580 --> 00:32:21.880
If nothing is done...

437
00:32:22.020 --> 00:32:23.240
Grandfather and everyone will...

438
00:32:23.240 --> 00:32:27.300
Sogeking-senpai! Run!

439
00:32:37.300 --> 00:32:38.680
Pirate Hunter!

440
00:32:40.260 --> 00:32:41.980
How long will you make me wait?!

441
00:32:42.080 --> 00:32:43.240
Hey, Director!

442
00:32:43.340 --> 00:32:46.260
Huh? If you mean "Commodore," that's me.

443
00:32:46.420 --> 00:32:47.620
Whatever!

444
00:32:47.940 --> 00:32:50.440
Didn't you throw someone like a cannonball earlier?

445
00:32:54.440 --> 00:32:57.260
Prepare yourself, King Riku!

446
00:32:59.220 --> 00:33:00.740
Shoot! Shoot!

447
00:33:13.640 --> 00:33:16.220
Your target is me, isn't it?!

448
00:33:16.640 --> 00:33:20.120
Please stop causing all this destruction!

449
00:33:23.680 --> 00:33:28.720
Everyone, out of here, now!
Evacuate the plateau!

450
00:33:37.100 --> 00:33:39.820
King Riku, you must leave too!

451
00:33:40.980 --> 00:33:42.740
Hurry, Father!

452
00:33:42.920 --> 00:33:46.360
Viola, Tank!
Take everyone and descend at once!

453
00:33:46.900 --> 00:33:49.400
His target is me! Go!

454
00:33:50.020 --> 00:33:52.520
That's why you need to run, King Riku!

455
00:33:52.820 --> 00:33:53.820
Please make haste!

456
00:33:54.360 --> 00:33:59.720
No! If everyone else can escape
while he's targeting me,

457
00:33:59.880 --> 00:34:01.260
then so be it!

458
00:34:03.340 --> 00:34:08.300
I see! Then I'll do as you ask!

459
00:34:18.500 --> 00:34:19.560
What the hell?

460
00:34:19.760 --> 00:34:23.300
Pirate Hunter, Orlumbus!
Just what are you doing?

461
00:34:23.480 --> 00:34:25.260
You really sure about this?

462
00:34:25.680 --> 00:34:28.960
This technique isn't meant for throwing someone safely!

463
00:34:29.320 --> 00:34:31.420
Just do it already! We don't have time!

464
00:34:31.720 --> 00:34:33.120
That bastard!

465
00:34:33.260 --> 00:34:35.920
He's only going after people
who don't want to fight!

466
00:34:36.060 --> 00:34:36.940
Ready?

467
00:34:37.280 --> 00:34:37.900
Yeah!

468
00:34:41.620 --> 00:34:45.120
King Riku! You are no king!

469
00:34:45.420 --> 00:34:47.920
You're not even fit to be king!

470
00:34:49.400 --> 00:34:53.120
Commodore...

471
00:35:05.420 --> 00:35:09.620
Your Majesty, if you won't run, then neither shall we!

472
00:35:09.720 --> 00:35:15.800
King Riku, did you clear up the decade-long misunderstanding and win back your popularity?

473
00:35:17.180 --> 00:35:20.660
A pacifist like you...

474
00:35:20.840 --> 00:35:24.800
couldn't even protect his country!
Or have you forgotten?

475
00:35:25.220 --> 00:35:27.040
A country is all about armed might!

476
00:35:27.380 --> 00:35:30.020
A man that can't destroy his country's enemies...

477
00:35:30.140 --> 00:35:33.220
is not qualified to be king!

478
00:35:35.040 --> 00:35:39.720
I'll pulverize you and your cheap ideals!

479
00:35:39.880 --> 00:35:42.260
King Riku!

480
00:35:45.760 --> 00:35:48.640
Th-The town is falling!

481
00:35:54.500 --> 00:35:57.360
Killer...

482
00:35:57.420 --> 00:35:58.560
Bowling!

483
00:36:19.540 --> 00:36:20.740
You're right!

484
00:36:20.860 --> 00:36:25.820
I couldn't protect my country, so I'm incompetent! I have no intention of sitting on the throne ever again!

485
00:36:26.000 --> 00:36:27.020
King Riku!

486
00:36:27.120 --> 00:36:28.060
However...

487
00:36:28.520 --> 00:36:31.440
I tried my best to be a good man!

488
00:36:37.620 --> 00:36:39.460
The nine mountains and eight seas...

489
00:36:40.000 --> 00:36:41.160
make one world!

490
00:36:41.800 --> 00:36:44.820
A thousand of them form a small chiliocosm!

491
00:36:41.800 --> 00:36:50.040
Note: Chiliocosm - Buddhist term for a cluster of a thousand realms.

492
00:36:45.580 --> 00:36:50.040
And when I gather and cube that chiliocosm, there's nothing I can't cut!

493
00:36:53.380 --> 00:36:55.780
Three-Sword Style Secret Technique!

494
00:36:57.040 --> 00:36:59.560
"Be a good man"?

495
00:36:59.660 --> 00:37:03.540
If you say I'm not allowed to live without committing murder,

496
00:37:04.260 --> 00:37:06.700
then I choose death!

497
00:37:07.320 --> 00:37:10.340
There's no future for a mass-murdering nation!

498
00:37:10.740 --> 00:37:14.240
Your Majesty! You are our one true king!

499
00:37:17.300 --> 00:37:21.640
This is why the good never make history!

500
00:37:22.120 --> 00:37:26.480
Because they all die like you!

501
00:37:30.920 --> 00:37:33.040
Great Trichiliocosm...

502
00:37:34.100 --> 00:37:36.380
One Billion Worlds!

503
00:38:17.060 --> 00:38:19.080
Good! He's escaped into the upper body!

504
00:38:19.680 --> 00:38:20.740
Roronoa!

505
00:38:45.040 --> 00:38:47.620
Zoro!

506
00:38:55.280 --> 00:38:56.760
Dead stones...

507
00:38:57.440 --> 00:38:58.960
Living stones...

508
00:38:59.620 --> 00:39:05.200
No matter how many pieces I carve him into, his real body definitely has to be in one of them!

509
00:39:07.580 --> 00:39:09.140
He can't be in two pieces at once!

510
00:39:27.080 --> 00:39:29.760
Whaaat?!

511
00:39:44.960 --> 00:39:47.440
There's no ground in the air for him to hide in!

512
00:39:50.520 --> 00:39:51.920
Show yourself, Pica!

513
00:40:04.200 --> 00:40:06.180
How long will you keep hiding?!

514
00:40:08.380 --> 00:40:09.840
By cornering me,

515
00:40:11.640 --> 00:40:13.220
you think you've already won?!

516
00:40:19.980 --> 00:40:25.400
You think you can beat me if you can cut those stones, don't you?

517
00:40:25.920 --> 00:40:28.880
I can't be cut when I'm clad in Haki!

518
00:40:34.210 --> 00:40:35.040
Haki, huh?

519
00:40:35.500 --> 00:40:39.020
If I knock you off, you lose!

520
00:40:39.920 --> 00:40:43.400
Only if your Haki is stronger than mine!

521
00:40:43.400 --> 00:40:47.700
I don't have time to stumble over you here!

522
00:40:47.800 --> 00:40:49.500
Quit babbling!

523
00:40:52.260 --> 00:40:54.000
The nine mountains and eight seas...

524
00:40:54.480 --> 00:40:55.980
There's nothing I can't cut!

525
00:40:56.380 --> 00:40:58.500
Die!

526
00:40:58.500 --> 00:41:01.050
Roronoa Zoro!

527
00:41:01.050 --> 00:41:02.720
Three Thousand Worlds!

528
00:41:07.710 --> 00:41:10.470
Stop troubling the innocent!

529
00:41:11.490 --> 00:41:13.850
Zoro-senpai!

530
00:41:14.870 --> 00:41:16.510
Doro!

531
00:41:20.230 --> 00:41:25.650
The Pirate Hunter... saved my friend, King Riku?

532
00:41:32.050 --> 00:41:35.450
It's still collapsing on us!

533
00:41:35.590 --> 00:41:39.790
We're gonna die!

534
00:41:40.030 --> 00:41:43.290
Help us, Boro!

535
00:41:49.070 --> 00:41:50.230
Your turn!

536
00:41:54.970 --> 00:41:56.730
King...

537
00:41:56.890 --> 00:41:59.630
Punch!

538
00:42:27.010 --> 00:42:30.250
That brat... He used my King Punch...

539
00:42:30.510 --> 00:42:33.130
to clear away some rocks! How rude!

540
00:42:33.490 --> 00:42:34.950
I won't forget this!

541
00:42:35.770 --> 00:42:37.210
That's that!
